Viewer: back from the reverse camera without a reconnect; one tap goes back to fullscreen (2026-10-12).

On the Xpeng G6 the reverse camera hides the browser, which comes back out of fullscreen. The page then
renegotiated the picture for the smaller window, a CarPlay restart of several seconds, and once more when
fullscreen was entered again. A browser enters fullscreen only on a tap, so the page cannot do it by itself.
Now an exit from fullscreen within 2 s of the page being hidden keeps the negotiated picture (shown scaled)
and the next tap on the picture goes back to fullscreen instead of reaching CarPlay ("轻点画面恢复全屏");
leaving fullscreen on purpose works as before. When the page is shown again it asks for a keyframe at once.
The viewer log gets page events right away (ev 1 hidden, 2 shown, 3 fullscreen, 4 out of fullscreen) and
counts music the car paused (musicSysPauses: another app took the sound).

